Subject: Drop the shared ColorBuffers when no guest process is left

The guest numbers its gralloc buffers from 1 each time Android starts, and every process
derives the ColorBuffer handle from that number. The renderer outlives the guest (it belongs to
the window manager), and the buffers the last Android left behind stayed: a process that opened
the new buffer 21 found the old buffer 21, at the old window's size, and kept it. SurfaceFlinger
then made an image of the new size on it, the host refused ("attempted to create a VkImage with
width:900 by importing ColorBuffer which only has width:640"), and the window stayed black.

dropSharedColorBuffers erases every ColorBuffer whose handle has the top bit set, whatever its
reference count. The renderer calls it when the last guest process pipe ends, which only
happens when the guest is gone.

Applies after 0043 on gfxstream d047a57228332d995d36600792fa9ccc26cf8ae6.
---
diff --git a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
--- a/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
+++ b/host/FrameBuffer.cpp
@@ -1446,6 +1446,22 @@
     AutoLock colorBufferMapLock(m_colorBufferMapLock);
     const size_t after = m_colorbuffers.size();
     return after < before ? static_cast<int>(before - after) : 0;
+}
+
+int FrameBuffer::dropSharedColorBuffers() {
+    AutoLock mutex(m_lock);
+    AutoLock colorBufferMapLock(m_colorBufferMapLock);
+    int dropped = 0;
+    for (auto it = m_colorbuffers.begin(); it != m_colorbuffers.end();) {
+        if (it->first & 0x80000000u) {
+            eraseDelayedCloseColorBufferLocked(it->first, it->second.closedTs);
+            it = m_colorbuffers.erase(it);
+            dropped++;
+        } else {
+            ++it;
+        }
+    }
+    return dropped;
 }
 
 std::vector<FrameBuffer::ColorBufferDescription> FrameBuffer::describeColorBuffers() {
diff --git a/host/FrameBuffer.h b/host/FrameBuffer.h
--- a/host/FrameBuffer.h
+++ b/host/FrameBuffer.h
@@ -242,6 +242,12 @@
     // otherwise stayed until another buffer was closed. Returns how many were destroyed. An
     // embedder calls it now and then.
     int closeDelayedColorBuffers();
+
+    // Erases every ColorBuffer a guest process shares (its handle has the top bit set), whatever
+    // its reference count. For the moment no guest process is left: the guest's buffer numbers
+    // start again from 1 when Android starts again, and a buffer the last Android left behind
+    // would be opened under a new buffer's number at the old one's size. Returns how many.
+    int dropSharedColorBuffers();
 
     // One live ColorBuffer as a memory report lists it: its size and format, the bytes of its
     // Vulkan memory, which guest process made it and when, the guest processes that hold it
